@bio:

	Anna Maria Matuszewska is an assistant professor at the
	Institute of Art of the Polish Academy of Sciences,
	specializing in digital musicology. She received her
	doctoral degree through the Binationale Promotion
	programme, jointly conducted at the Institute of Literary
	Research of the Polish Academy of Sciences and the
	Karlsruhe University of Music. Her research focuses on user
	experience (UX) in the context of musicological tools, with
	the aim of developing an analytical interface for
	comparative studies of the European ballad.

@@END: BIO